# Generated benchmark fixtures and harness scratch directories.
# These are regenerated on every sweep run and must never be committed: they
# hide real work in `git status` and each one is tens to hundreds of MB.
bench_tmp*/
bt_*/
bt_b75a/
bt_d1024/
bt_synth/

# Harness logs. The receipts under receipts/ are the authority; raw .log/.err
# captures are diagnostic only and several are corrupted by concurrent runs.
*.log
*.err
src/masm/disasm.txt
src/masm/cf_disasm.txt
src/masm/gp.txt

# Local build scratch for the ad-hoc sweep/probe toolchain (regime_sweep and
# friends are built by hand into the repo root, not by CMake).
rs*.exe
b79.exe
cf_probe*.exe
gguf_probe.exe
gguf_memory.exe

# CMake/VS build scratch trees. Regenerated by every configure; thousands of
# .vcxproj/.tlog/CMakeCache files that bury real source in diffs.
cmlink/
certbuild/
.repo_intel_cache/
